&lt;p&gt;Lumen Ledger builds reconciliation and month-end close software for small finance teams. Our customers are accountants at 20-to-200-person companies who are tired of matching bank lines in spreadsheets. We are a remote team of 34 spread across EMEA and South Asia, and we are hiring our second junior backend engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain Node.js and TypeScript services that import bank feeds and match transactions to invoices.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Write PostgreSQL migrations and tune the queries behind our matching engine.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ship small, well-tested changes to production several times a week, with review from a senior engineer.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Join a light, daytime-only support rotation once you are settled in.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Must have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;At least 1 year of professional experience writing backend code in Node.js with TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL and relational data modelling, ideally PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Clear written English; most of our collaboration is asynchronous.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;At least four hours of overlap with 09:00-17:00 CET.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Docker and Docker Compose.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Some AWS exposure (RDS, ECS or Lambda).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;An interest in accounting or payments.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation and location&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fully remote within EMEA and South Asia (UTC-1 to UTC+6). Salary USD 28,000-36,000 per year depending on location and experience, paid monthly through our employer-of-record partner, plus a USD 600 yearly learning budget and a home-office stipend.&lt;/p&gt;
